sf-faction-a-seraph-name = Angels: Seraphic Synod
sf-faction-a-seraph-description = Charged precision volleys after standing still for three seconds. Superweapon: Spear of First Light.
sf-faction-a-warden-name = Angels: Order of the Gate
sf-faction-a-warden-description = Gatekeepers and Wardbearers protect nearby allies; formation trades speed for armor. Superweapon: The Unbroken Gate.
sf-faction-a-exile-name = Angels: The Unshackled
sf-faction-a-exile-description = Below half health, outcasts gain firepower and speed; exposed survivors reward aggressive retreats. Superweapon: Heaven in Revolt.
sf-faction-h-bastion-name = Humans: Bastion Directorate
sf-faction-h-bastion-description = After four seconds stationary, troops entrench for armor and range; moving breaks the position. Superweapon: Rolling Thunder.
sf-faction-h-union-name = Humans: Free Earth Union
sf-faction-h-union-description = Harvesters and Pathfinders project mobile supply corridors: faster movement and reloads. Superweapon: Emergency Airlift.
sf-faction-h-covenant-name = Humans: Ashen Covenant
sf-faction-h-covenant-description = Templars and Confessors heal nearby infantry and harden their resolve. Superweapon: Ashes to Ashes.
sf-faction-d-legion-name = Demons: Iron Legions
sf-faction-d-legion-description = Hellreavers and Taskmasters bind nearby troops into slow, armored siege formations. Superweapon: The Ninth Furnace.
sf-faction-d-brood-name = Demons: Blood Brood
sf-faction-d-brood-description = Enemy mobile-unit kills feed the killer: healing and six seconds of faster strikes; buildings grant no feeding. Superweapon: The Red Deluge.
sf-faction-d-court-name = Demons: Court of Whispers
sf-faction-d-court-description = Hexers and Silencers curse enemies with slow movement and weakened damage for four seconds. Superweapon: The Nameless Silence.
sf-faction-random-name = Random Sevenfall Faction
sf-faction-random-description = Choose one of the twelve playable hosts at random.

sf-a-spire-name = Radiant Spire
sf-a-spire-description = Celestial power generation; costly but efficient.
sf-h-generator-name = Veil Generator
sf-h-generator-description = Inexpensive industrial generator.
sf-d-heart-name = Furnace Heart
sf-d-heart-description = Infernal power organ grown from Veilglass.
sf-a-veilworks-name = Sanctification Crucible
sf-a-veilworks-description = Processes Veilglass; includes a Gatherer.
sf-h-veilworks-name = Fracture Refinery
sf-h-veilworks-description = Refines Veilglass; includes a Harvester.
sf-d-veilworks-name = Maw of Want
sf-d-veilworks-description = Consumes Veilglass; includes a Devourer.
sf-a-chapel-name = Choir Citadel
sf-a-chapel-description = Trains celestial warriors.
sf-h-barracks-name = Survival Barracks
sf-h-barracks-description = Trains human infantry.
sf-d-pit-name = Birthing Pit
sf-d-pit-description = Spawns lesser infernal infantry.
sf-a-armory-name = Heavenforge
sf-a-armory-description = Assembles elite celestial war engines.
sf-h-motorpool-name = Motor Pool
sf-h-motorpool-description = Manufactures mechanized human vehicles.
sf-d-forge-name = Flesh Forge
sf-d-forge-description = Grows infernal siege creatures.

sf-a-watcher-name = Watcher
sf-a-watcher-description = Elite line infantry: durable radiant volleys and Renewal. Expensive, slow to replace; shorter range than human rifles.
sf-h-rifleman-name = Rifleman
sf-h-rifleman-description = Cost-efficient sustained rifle fire with superior line-infantry range. Fragile when surrounded; poor against armour.
sf-d-thrall-name = Thrall
sf-d-thrall-description = Cheap, fragile melee infantry. Fast production; attacking triggers Blood Frenzy. Vulnerable before closing range.
sf-a-judicator-name = Judicator
sf-a-judicator-description = Durable anti-armour/air specialist with heavy, slow missiles and Renewal. Human rockets outrange it.
sf-h-rocketeer-name = Rocketeer
sf-h-rocketeer-description = Long-range, rapid anti-tank/air rockets. Less durable and less damage per missile than a Judicator.
sf-d-cinderling-name = Cinderling
sf-d-cinderling-description = Short-range incendiary specialist against infantry and wooden structures. Fragile; attacking triggers Blood Frenzy.
sf-a-aegis-name = Aegis Engine
sf-a-aegis-description = Durable precision war engine with heavy anti-armour volleys and Renewal. Slow and expensive.
sf-h-bulwark-name = Bulwark Tank
sf-h-bulwark-description = Cost-efficient tank with long-range sustained cannon fire and 50% faster depot repair. Less durable than Angel engines.
sf-d-ravager-name = Ravager Beast
sf-d-ravager-description = Fast melee anti-armour beast. Blood Frenzy rewards closing distance; vulnerable to ranged focus fire.
sf-a-seraphim-name = Seraphim
sf-a-seraphim-description = Synod-exclusive radiant area fire and heavy anti-air missiles; Renewal. Costly and slow.
sf-a-gatekeeper-name = Gatekeeper
sf-a-gatekeeper-description = Order-exclusive fortress engine: exceptional durability, heavy volleys and Renewal; very slow.
sf-a-penitent-name = Penitent
sf-a-penitent-description = Unshackled-exclusive mobile raider with Renewal; lighter armour and shorter range than other Angels.
sf-h-siegegun-name = Siege Cannon
sf-h-siegegun-description = Bastion-exclusive artillery with the longest combat-unit range and faster depot repair. Fragile; four-cell minimum range.
sf-h-ranger-name = Wasteland Ranger
sf-h-ranger-description = Union-exclusive fast scout with long-range precision rifle fire. Light armour; poor against tanks.
sf-h-templar-name = Ash Templar
sf-h-templar-description = Covenant-exclusive armoured missile infantry. Stronger individual shots but slower fire than Rocketeers.
sf-d-hellreaver-name = Hellreaver
sf-d-hellreaver-description = Legion-exclusive heavy melee siege beast. Strong against armour and structures; Blood Frenzy, no ranged attack.
sf-d-skitter-name = Skitter
sf-d-skitter-description = Brood-exclusive cheapest, fastest melee swarm. Blood Frenzy; extremely fragile and ineffective against heavy armour.
sf-d-hexer-name = Hexer
sf-d-hexer-description = Court-exclusive short-range curse caster with a separate anti-air spell. Blood Frenzy; fragile under direct fire.
sf-a-gatherer-name = Celestial Gatherer
sf-a-gatherer-description = Slow and resilient Veilglass collector.
sf-h-harvester-name = Industrial Harvester
sf-h-harvester-description = Balanced Veilglass collector with 50% faster depot repair. Requires a staffed economy to replace losses.
sf-d-devourer-name = Infernal Devourer
sf-d-devourer-description = Fast but fragile Veilglass collector.

