# Sevenfall defense roster
sf-a-dawnwall-name = Wall of Dawn
sf-a-dawnwall-description = Passable to allies; a powered light curtain incinerates hostile ground units that try to cross. Cut power or attack from range.
sf-a-sanctuary-name = Sanctuary Beacon
sf-a-sanctuary-description = Heals nearby allied infantry and prevents Mourning Flesh conversion within four cells. Requires power.
sf-a-watchfire-name = Watchfire Bastion
sf-a-watchfire-description = Rapid halo bolts suppress infantry; less effective against heavy armor. Requires power.
sf-a-judgment-name = Judgment Lance
sf-a-judgment-description = Long-range radiant lance strikes armor slowly. Vulnerable to infantry swarms and power cuts.
sf-a-skyward-name = Skyward Choir
sf-a-skyward-description = Guided celestial bolts intercept aircraft; cannot attack ground units. Requires power.
sf-h-blastwall-name = Bastion Blast Wall
sf-h-blastwall-description = Reinforced modular wall blocks ground movement and projectiles; siege weapons and heavy crushers can breach it.
sf-h-razorwire-name = Razorwire Entanglement
sf-h-razorwire-description = Enemy infantry are slowed to 65 percent speed and cut while crossing. Ground vehicles crush the wire.
sf-h-entrenchment-name = Resistance Entrenchment
sf-h-entrenchment-description = Three infantry can occupy this fortified firing position. Empty positions do not shoot; occupants supply their weapons.
sf-h-autocannon-name = Bastion Autocannon
sf-h-autocannon-description = Reliable rapid-fire kinetic defense against infantry and light armor; operates through power failures.
sf-h-missilenest-name = Skyguard Missile Nest
sf-h-missilenest-description = Dedicated guided anti-air missiles; crewed backup controls keep it working without power.
sf-d-mourningwall-name = Mourning Flesh
sf-d-mourningwall-description = Regenerating flesh wall. Its powered moans convert enemy infantry after 12 seconds of sustained exposure within three cells; retreat or Sanctuary counters it.
sf-d-thornfield-name = Bloodthorn Snare
sf-d-thornfield-description = Living thorns slow enemy infantry to half speed and bleed them while crossing. Vehicles crush the growth.
sf-d-spinenest-name = Spine Nest
sf-d-spinenest-description = A living organ spits bone spines into infantry. Ineffective against heavy armor; requires power.
sf-d-cindermaw-name = Cinder Maw
sf-d-cindermaw-description = A short-range infernal furnace burns armored attackers; outrange it with artillery. Requires power.
sf-d-skyhook-name = Skyhook Reliquary
sf-d-skyhook-description = Living guided skyhooks attack aircraft only; requires power.

sf-cottage-name = Civilian Cottage
sf-townhouse-name = Civilian Townhouse
sf-house-description = Move infantry beside an empty house to claim it, then enter to garrison. Force-fire to destroy. Engineers repair surviving houses.
sf-bridge-name = Stone Bridge
sf-bridge-description = Destructible crossing. Destroying the deck blocks ground passage. Send an engineer to the repair post to restore it.
sf-bridge-post-name = Bridge Repair Post
sf-bridge-post-description = Send an engineer here to repair or rebuild the linked bridge.
sf-engineer-description = Unarmed repair specialist. Repairs damaged civilian houses and restores bridges at their repair posts. Reusable after repair.
sf-a-engineer-name = Angelic Restorer
sf-h-engineer-name = Human Field Engineer
sf-d-engineer-name = Infernal Mason
sf-mcv-alpha-name = Mobile Construction Vehicle
sf-mcv-alpha-description = Deploys into a Construction Yard. Requires a Service Depot.

# Additional subfaction doctrines
sf-a-congregant-name = Ashbound Congregant
sf-a-congregant-description = Cheap human worshipper. Within five cells of a Cantor or Processional Shrine, Conviction reduces damage and prevents dread. Enemy-caused deaths charge nearby Choir angels: three stacks maximum, six seconds.
sf-a-cantor-name = Cantor of Desolation
sf-a-cantor-description = Angelic overseer. Grants Conviction to nearby worshippers and enables Last Hymn martyrdom within five cells. Kill or isolate the Cantor to break the formation.
sf-h-retrieval-name = Retrieval Team
sf-h-retrieval-description = Black-site reconnaissance infantry with eight-cell sight and short-range cloak detection. Screens expensive experimental vehicles. Sample recovery remains future research.
sf-h-janus-name = Janus Tank
sf-h-janus-description = Experimental containment tank. SERAPH fires long-range precision shots; ABYSS delivers short-range infernal fire. A powered Containment Pylon is required. Protocol changes disable firing for three seconds.
sf-d-magistrate-name = Magistrate of Ash
sf-d-magistrate-description = Attacking pronounces Contempt: one visible target per player, ten-second mark, eight-second retarget cooldown. Circle attacks deal 15% extra damage; killing the condemned enemy grants six seconds of Ascendancy. Killing the Magistrate cancels the mark.
sf-d-contemptor-name = Contemptor
sf-d-contemptor-description = Armored close-range execution beast. Strong against damaged heavy targets; weak against cheap infantry screens. Gains 30% execution damage against targets below half health.
sf-a-processional-name = Processional Shrine
sf-a-processional-description = Powered four-person garrison and hymn relay. Extends Conviction and enables martyrdom within five cells. Empty shrines cannot shoot.
sf-h-containment-name = Containment Pylon
sf-h-containment-description = Powered null field suppresses Renewal, Blood Frenzy, dread and doctrine buffs within four cells, including friendly supernatural abilities. Select and Deploy (F) to switch SERAPH/ABYSS; oldest powered pylon controls your Janus tanks. Switching takes three seconds.
sf-d-throne-name = Throne of Scorn
sf-d-throne-description = Powered organic defense and command monument. If both attacker and its living Magistrate stand within five cells, condemnation damage rises from 15% to 30%.
sf-faction-a-desolation-name = Choir of Desolation
sf-faction-a-desolation-description = Human Congregant deaths empower angels inside Cantor and Shrine hymn networks. Superweapon: Requiem for the Living.
sf-faction-h-area52-name = Area Fifty Two
sf-faction-h-area52-description = Powered containment switches Janus weapons between SERAPH and ABYSS; null fields suppress supernatural abilities. Superweapon: Project Event Horizon.
sf-faction-d-contempt-name = Circle of Contempt
sf-faction-d-contempt-description = Magistrates condemn priority targets; Contemptors punish wounded enemies and executions grant Ascendancy. Superweapon: The Final Verdict.
